    "title": "Who's in national championship game? Updated Frozen Four bracket, NCAA Tournament schedule",
    "text": "April 9, 2026Updated April 10, 2026, 3:12 p.m. ETThe national championship stage has been set for the 2026 NCAA men's hockey tournament.Wisconsin pulled off a 2-1 win over No. 2 North Dakota in the first semifinal of the 2026 Frozen Four on Thursday, April 9, from T-Mobile Arena in Las Vegas.Wisconsin scored two goals within less than a minute of each other in the first period and then held on for the rest of the way for the victory. Simon Tassy opened the scoring off an assist from Vasily Zelenov at the 12:54 mark, and then Ryan Botterill added a goal off assists from Joe Palodichuk and Ben Dexheimer at 13:21.Ellis Rickwood scored the lone goal for North Dakota with 52 seconds remaining in the third period, to make things interesting at the end.Wisconsin's last national title came in 2006 and the Badgers have six in program history.The Badgers' opponent is Denver, which beat No. 1 national seed Michigan 4-3, in double overtime, thanks to Kent Anderson's go-ahead goal in the sudden-victory double overtime period.Here's a look at who will be playing in the NCAA men's Frozen Four national championship in 2026:Who's in national championship? Updated Frozen Four bracketWisconsin became the first team to earn a bid to the 2026 men's Frozen Four championship game with its 2-1 win over North Dakota.Denver later joined the Badgers after the Pioneers survived an odyssey against No. 1 seed Michigan as their match went deep into the night.NCAA Frozen Four national championship schedule, game time, TV info, locationThe men's NCAA tournament championship will be held at T-Mobile Arena in Las Vegas.Saturday, April 11Wisconsin vs. Denver | 5:30 p.m. ET | ESPN | Fubo (free trial)Frozen Four 2026 bracket updateRegional semifinalsWorcester:No. 3 Michigan State 2, UConn 1Wisconsin 5, Dartmouth 1Sioux Falls:Quinnipiac 5, Providence 2No. 2 North Dakota 3, Merrimack 0Loveland:No. 4 Western Michigan 3, Minnesota State 1Denver 5, Cornell 0Albany:No. 1 Michigan 5, Bentley 1Minnesota-Duluth 3, Penn State 1Regional finalsWorcester: Wisconsin 4, No. 3 Michigan State 3 (OT)Sioux Falls: No. 2 North Dakota 5, Quinnipiac 0Loveland final: Denver 6, No. 4 Western Michigan 2Albany final: No. 1 Michigan 4, Minnesota-Duluth 3Frozen FourNational semifinal Game 1: Wisconsin 2, No. 2 North Dakota 1National semifinal Game 2: Denver 4, No. 1 Michigan 3 (2OT)Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
